* PIC16(L)F1827 Pin Definitions -- 18-Pin PDIP/SOIC, 20-Pin SSOP,
* and 28-Pin QFN (combined)
* Source: Microchip DS41391D "PIC16(L)F1826/27 Data Sheet" (full
*         datasheet, superseding the DS41363A Advance-Information
*         product brief this file was originally built from), Pin
*         Diagrams section and Table 1-2 (Pinout Description).
*
* Primary device: PIC16F1827 -- determines this file's name.
*
* Companion device -- PIC16LF1827 differs only in operating voltage
* range (1.8-3.6V vs 1.8-5.5V), same as every other "L" variant in
* this project. Table 1 confirms PIC16F1827 and PIC16LF1827 have
* identical Flash/EEPROM/SRAM/I-O/ADC/timer/EUSART/MSSP/CCP/CapSense
* specs -- differ only in voltage/speed grade. Both included:
*   PIC16F1827, PIC16LF1827
*
* NOT included -- PIC16F1826/PIC16LF1826, despite sharing this same
* document (this full datasheet, like the product brief before it,
* covers both devices together), the exact same pin diagrams, and
* the exact same 16 physical GPIO pins (RA0-RA7, RB0-RB7). Confirmed
* directly (not just inferred from the product brief) by this
* datasheet's own Table 1-2 Note 2: "Functions are only available on
* the PIC16(L)F1827" -- covering CCP2, CCP3, CCP4, P2A, P2B, SDA2,
* SCL2, SCK2, SDI2, SDO2, and SS2. Several pins genuinely do less on
* the 1826. This fails this project's pin-compatibility bar ("never
* differ ... in peripheral pin assignments"), so 1826/LF1826 need
* their own separate file if wanted later.
*
* Package scope -- ALL THREE packages (18-pin PDIP/SOIC, 20-pin SSOP,
* 28-pin QFN) are combined into this single file, same pattern as
* PIC16F1847 (same product family/generation): Table 2's peripheral/
* alternate-function columns are pin-name-based, not package-specific,
* and the only differences between package pin COUNTS are duplicate
* VDD/VSS pins (18-pin: 1+1; 20-pin: 2+2; 28-pin: 2+2) plus 6 NC pins
* filling out the 28-pin QFN body. No package adds a new signal pin.
*
* Flagged for manual review (dual-function / non-obvious pins):
*   RA5     -- MCLR/VPP/SS1. Table 1-2 confirms explicitly (same
*             wording/format as every other port pin): "RA5 TTL CMOS
*             General purpose I/O." Classified B (not I): the MCLRE
*             config bit allows RA5 to be ordinary GPIO when the
*             dedicated Reset function is disabled.
*   RA6/RA7 -- OSC2/CLKOUT/... and OSC1/CLKIN/..., oscillator-mode-
*             dependent alternate functions on otherwise ordinary
*             GPIO pins (external clock/crystal mode is a config-bit
*             choice, not a pin dedication). Classified B, same
*             reasoning as PIC16F1847's RA6/RA7.
*   RB6/RB7 -- likely datasheet naming inconsistency, same pattern
*             already flagged in PIC16F1847.qpindef: the RB6 pin-name
*             header lists "T1OSI" (Timer1 Oscillator Input), but
*             Table 1-2's function breakdown for RB6 lists "T1OSO"
*             (Timer1 Oscillator Output) -- the same name the
*             breakdown also gives RB7. Recorded as T1OSI for RB6
*             (trusting the header, matching the expected T1OSI/T1OSO
*             crystal-pair convention). This is evidently a template
*             artifact shared across the whole PIC16F182x/184x
*             document family, not a one-off typo -- it appears
*             identically in the PIC16F1847 datasheet. Verify against
*             the family reference manual if Timer1 async oscillator
*             mode matters for your use case.
*   RB0     -- also includes FLT0 (ECCP Auto-Shutdown Fault input),
*             present in this full datasheet's Table 1-2 but missing
*             from the DS41363A product brief's compact pin table --
*             this file now includes it.
*   RB0-RB7 -- all individually support interrupt-on-change (IOC)
*             with an individually enabled weak pull-up; a shared
*             electrical feature of the whole port, not a separate
*             alternate function requiring its own field.
*
* All other pins are ordinary GPIO pins with ADC/comparator/
* capacitive-sensing/PWM/EUSART/MSSP alternate functions, several
* relocatable to one of two pin locations via software (marked in
* the source diagrams but not separately encoded here, same as the
* dsPIC/PIC16F1847 RPn-style remap notes elsewhere in this project).
* Classified B.

D PIC16(L)F1827 18/20/28-Pin PDIP/SOIC/SSOP/QFN 8-bit Flash Microcontroller
P PIC16F1827 PIC16LF1827

V VDD
B RA0 AN0/CPS0/C12IN0-/SDO2
B RA1 AN1/CPS1/C12IN1-/SS2
B RA2 AN2/CPS2/C12IN2-/C12IN+/VREF-/DACOUT
B RA3 AN3/CPS3/C12IN3-/C1IN+/VREF+/C1OUT/CCP3/SRQ
B RA4 AN4/CPS4/C2OUT/T0CKI/CCP4/SRNQ
B RA5 MCLR/VPP/SS1
B RA6 OSC2/CLKOUT/CLKR/P1D/P2B/SDO1
X 1
K SIMCLK

B RA7 OSC1/CLKIN/P1C/CCP2/P2A
B RB0 INT/SRI/T1G/CCP1/P1A/FLT0
B RB1 AN11/CPS11/RX/DT/SDA1/SDI1
B RB2 AN10/CPS10/MDMIN/RX/DT/TX/CK/SDA2/SDI2/SDO1
B RB3 AN9/CPS9/MDOUT/CCP1/P1A
B RB4 AN8/CPS8/SCL1/SCK1/MDCIN2
B RB5 AN7/CPS7/P1B/TX/CK/SCL2/SCK2/SS1
B RB6 AN5/CPS5/T1CKI/T1OSCI/P1C/CCP2/P2A/ICSPCLK
B RB7 AN6/CPS6/T1OSCO/P1D/P2B/MDCIN1/ICSPDAT
G VSS
